ulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "595cbfc4-8fff-5045-9e69-dae0c1acb047" :question/math-academy-id "q-134009" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f64050151e65151975954cdf169379c5ea6ee80b0348a6cb03706ab64c7c7105.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](images/00/00fe583ae8b83bfef31c1914489be7794aa4b7b2850cd01243a46b8d86d1dddb.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e1f18b-1852-5af1-8499-7eb19e018ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266308} {:answer/id #uuid "184cd861-8c34-5268-9a33-ee4b1a82e271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266345} {:answer/id #uuid "1b7a5941-b902-5459-89a3-423d6555f39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266378} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4d098a-9ed0-542a-ad02-61052de5a409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266673} {:answer/id #uuid "f25133e5-029a-5434-834e-2ae8f93904ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12e1f18b-1852-5af1-8499-7eb19e018ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266308} :answer-field/id #uuid "06014dbd-b187-5859-8fef-b25bfa74ae6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2869212-3453-5179-ad24-03054774f50a" :question/math-academy-id "q-134011" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c55d326b26a8bb6831f38456b7b47878ef66a185090c7327cbb151c4e951be33.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02218168-6841-5f87-b459-2ef8ded18fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541429} {:answer/id #uuid "06efb0b9-ff81-5d60-949a-63d7901766a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541436} {:answer/id #uuid "1347198e-7062-5143-bac3-b619f4969e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541461} {:answer/id #uuid "4bcba26e-b5e7-51d8-9a3e-8c8e00c7d593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541578} {:answer/id #uuid "a0deb69e-60ce-5af0-98d7-4bcde1e624aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bcba26e-b5e7-51d8-9a3e-8c8e00c7d593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541578} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b478d5-40d3-56c6-919f-e4aca770b60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38830f71-0f2a-562f-b716-243d080e51d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-134012" :question/problem "![](images/60/60b546c0e2d37362fefde1023ed093d2f544b187742bb690d5fe60bc417b48d4.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,5).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-2}{3-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17356e8d-52ec-5267-88b4-0e420beef0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541469} {:answer/id #uuid "2d252d8c-d493-5170-b7a6-d761bb5e5e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541511} {:answer/id #uuid "44453f11-c660-507e-a6a0-3784729b906d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541568} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa23fc9-19ad-5907-93ad-4b1a0885d020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541584} {:answer/id #uuid "c654e87c-750d-5151-96fc-24fd14b7437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{8}x+\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d252d8c-d493-5170-b7a6-d761bb5e5e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541511} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b9c6ec5-0c09-548c-8228-cf9708222788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94bd2cbd-504c-548c-9ed1-5e5adaadef48" :question/math-academy-id "q-134020" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b82ed81f724322dc05a2c65d3635ac74f5ca92ff413e9d7e5131ebb604269f26.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-4,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,3).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{4-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{3}{8}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{8}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(-4,6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{3}{8}x+b \\\\ 6 & =-\\frac{3}{8}(-4)+b \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{3}{2}+b \\\\ 12 & =3+2b \\\\ b & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3800c633-4663-5a7c-977b-4d0c6dda0f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266629} {:answer/id #uuid "53efa526-eb5e-5256-af09-1eec2833abff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266895} {:answer/id #uuid "aba8afc3-be94-5f08-8b22-73af4c6b41c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267693} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8916a0-dcf5-50b0-b591-84f24b525679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268274} {:answer/id #uuid "f31ff6ea-86e9-5bba-a3ed-309adf564a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aba8afc3-be94-5f08-8b22-73af4c6b41c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267693} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d24660-a466-52cd-ab29-3ad82a1272ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c42b7eb-86b2-59d5-8ce6-728291f9e718" :question/math-academy-id "q-134023" :question/problem "![](images/1c/1c9f30692222eaaed4cda6b608dcc1ccb01eefd6b5fa7730b5b8bb29c9f528b1.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,8).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{7-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=\\frac{6}{5}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{6}{5}x+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{6}{5}(2)+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{12}{5}+b \\\\ 10 & =12+5b \\\\ -2 & =5b \\\\ b & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f69d6d6-f65d-5ba2-a0d2-ec96450b904c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266563} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2b2005-e668-56d9-b3b4-b2d1d38ff629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266964} {:answer/id #uuid "99a06ebc-ac19-5f94-a156-eb204f48255f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267534} {:answer/id #uuid "a5340cd2-a9ed-55b6-9b11-313ff0af8372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267633} {:answer/id #uuid "e72106a0-7ad8-5146-bba3-a4016a76a043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f69d6d6-f65d-5ba2-a0d2-ec96450b904c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266563} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41ee374-e612-55c4-a15d-7afecd007c01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fec0ce3a-bf15-5c41-9f72-214fd8c31558" :question/math-academy-id "q-134025" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c8f6d0161777412704a9a80c0336af04a6968454d421913055024b6d0cf11c71.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/b5/b50fd1636cc2e1bb9d150eaba9cc25a3ccedff77e607bf22853004332a7c4ddc.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(3,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(5,3).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{2} \\\\  & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36fff2b4-d8f8-5391-8f3d-f1aa18360507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541539} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3afe47-1165-5002-bbea-e6fcf3ae647c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541640} {:answer/id #uuid "82bb59f7-9705-5805-a312-3df68bf3cb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541687} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2f07ff-c342-5dcf-9ba3-e58cebd333c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541752} {:answer/id #uuid "f9568aff-bb94-59a7-a7e4-d94d894d808c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36fff2b4-d8f8-5391-8f3d-f1aa18360507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541539} :answer-field/id #uuid "db4bfec2-e156-5a49-b929-8f51580bf008" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07871eb6-b857-5072-89f4-ba9b4061b1b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134028" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2ddf870155c876bac41bd437229afb971bcb6eb6cdd67351c27a0132f7d05325.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/b7/b79dacf04634d91eae5ee8dd82a6603ed93357d6300a95e6343a683429caf506.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(4,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(8,4).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-6}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{4} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d7e6c7d-9523-5d3a-9512-3303d59336bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0.5x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541642} {:answer/id #uuid "965db60e-03bc-5816-9108-a20a96a20071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541735} {:answer/id #uuid "9737ccf3-fccb-59bd-8554-c4d39bf5417f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0.5x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541736} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5b411d-5258-56ac-82df-1a19c550b5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541855} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9fae53-d1eb-5b69-9068-61eacfbae378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9737ccf3-fccb-59bd-8554-c4d39bf5417f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0.5x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541736} :answer-field/id #uuid "16786d6f-ad61-5cf1-a755-78c7e48129ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f2a8490-6351-51db-83b8-81572c8b1d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-134029" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2154f7bdd31e0c35517051fe46764ab75e597d0d78dbc64ffc55d1faecbec78.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/68/687b257b9e2c6d3d2a015a5703d4fc29e9ab0598fb7e7ac69b588334c4a1e73d.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(6,6).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-4}{6-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.5x+b \\\\ 4 & =0.5(2)+b \\\\ 4 & =1+b \\\\ 3 & =b \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099bdefa-f8d2-5acc-84b7-74bc261996fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266231} {:answer/id #uuid "2ee57d74-67d5-5b61-af35-96dd84de092c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266560} {:answer/id #uuid "33b80c4e-3ce7-5308-9505-f492c7dd9012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266598} {:answer/id #uuid "90363514-ca92-5816-8b4b-8b82cf37e7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267426} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ad0a79-a3c4-5480-9db0-3f13ff4381f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2.5x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ee57d74-67d5-5b61-af35-96dd84de092c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266560} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d92bc77-95f8-5697-932c-a47df1e134b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "240005ae-034c-5e2f-9211-125231674030" :question/math-academy-id "q-134032" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d23d6a35343aebcb986118bd7c5bc720f00480706057ec900e55c75bac296ebb.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/66/663e4d77d51816641a9fa861f37893d9f986d5e2b00e605ed5eb4fc19d40eab4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(5,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(7,9).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-5}{7-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x+b \\\\ 5 & =2(5)+b \\\\ 5 & =10+b \\\\ -5 & =b \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=2x-5.\n$$"}]}
